<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Windows Sandbox configuration for the clean-machine installation test.

  Windows Sandbox starts from a pristine Windows image every time: no Python,
  no Qt, no Visual C++ build tools, no OMRFlow source. That is exactly the
  environment docs/release/CLEAN_MACHINE_TEST.md requires, and it removes the
  "was it really clean?" doubt that a reused virtual machine leaves behind.

  Usage
      1. Build the installer:   .\scripts\release\Build-Installer.ps1
      2. Run:                   .\packaging\sandbox\New-SandboxPayload.ps1 -Launch

  Do not launch this file directly. Step 2 stages the payload and writes
  OMRFlow-CleanMachine.generated.wsb beside it with the <HostFolder> path
  resolved to an absolute one, because whether Sandbox accepts a relative
  <HostFolder> depends on the Windows build. The generated file is the one
  that gets launched; this one is the version-controlled template.

  The payload folder is mapped READ-ONLY, so nothing the test does can reach
  back into it. Step 2 stages only the installer and the checksum file there
  - deliberately not the source tree, because an importable source tree is
  one of the two defects this test exists to catch.

  A second folder is mapped WRITABLE, for results only. A sandbox discards
  everything when it closes, so without it the evidence for the release would
  be a screenshot of a transcript. It is a separate folder, outside the
  repository, precisely so that "the payload is read-only" stays true: the
  test can report, but it cannot reach the installer it is testing or any
  source. Step 2 resolves both paths.

  Networking is disabled: OMRFlow must work with no network at all (there is
  no telemetry and no cloud upload), and a sandbox with no network cannot
  quietly download a missing runtime and mask a packaging defect. Note that
  this also means SmartScreen cannot appear, so step 5 of
  CLEAN_MACHINE_TEST.md is not observable here.
-->
<Configuration>
  <VGpu>Enable</VGpu>
  <Networking>Disable</Networking>

  <MappedFolders>
    <MappedFolder>
      <HostFolder>.\payload</HostFolder>
      <SandboxFolder>C:\Users\WDAGUtilityAccount\Desktop\OMRFlow</SandboxFolder>
      <ReadOnly>true</ReadOnly>
    </MappedFolder>
    <MappedFolder>
      <HostFolder>.\results</HostFolder>
      <SandboxFolder>C:\Users\WDAGUtilityAccount\Desktop\OMRFlow-results</SandboxFolder>
      <ReadOnly>false</ReadOnly>
    </MappedFolder>
  </MappedFolders>

  <LogonCommand>
    <Command>powershell.exe -NoProfile -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File C:\Users\WDAGUtilityAccount\Desktop\OMRFlow\Start-CleanMachineTest.ps1</Command>
  </LogonCommand>

  <MemoryInMB>8192</MemoryInMB>
  <AudioInput>Disable</AudioInput>
  <VideoInput>Disable</VideoInput>
  <ClipboardRedirection>Enable</ClipboardRedirection>
  <PrinterRedirection>Disable</PrinterRedirection>
  <ProtectedClient>Disable</ProtectedClient>
</Configuration>
